menu "OmniSensor Configuration"

    config OMNI_BATTERY_PRESENT
        bool "A LiPo cell and the battery divider are fitted"
        default n
        help
            Enable once the 2x100k divider and a LiPo cell are actually wired to
            GPIO0. With this off the firmware skips battery sampling entirely and
            reports mains/USB power, rather than publishing whatever noise an
            unconnected ADC pin happens to read. See docs/HARDWARE_DESIGN.md §3.

    config OMNI_LOAD_SWITCH_PRESENT
        bool "The SI2301 radar load switch is fitted"
        default n
        help
            Enable once the SI2301 and its gate pull-up are actually wired to
            GPIO21. With this off the radar is assumed to be permanently
            powered, which is what a breadboard with plain jumper wires gives
            you, and the firmware does not claim to be switching a rail that
            is not there. The presence session still starts and stops the UART
            either way. See hardware/DESIGN_PACKAGE.md §6.

endmenu
